# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Policy artifacts  [Addendum 1 section 4 — never-commit list]
#
# The scoring policy is proprietary. Only the demonstration pack may be
# committed. These rules are deliberately deny-by-default: a new policy file
# with an unanticipated name is blocked rather than allowed, because the cost
# of over-blocking is an explicit override and the cost of under-blocking is an
# irreversible disclosure.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
policy/*
!policy/README.md
!policy/demo.*.json
!policy/schema.json
!policy/BOUNDARY_DEBT.txt

# Production naming conventions, blocked explicitly wherever they appear
*.policy.json
*policy.prod*.json
*policy.production*.json
*.private.json
**/policy.prod*
**/policy.production*
**/*_policy_weights*

# Term legend and minting salt  [Addendum 1 section 2 — opaque aggregate terms]
#
# The legend maps opaque identifiers back to human labels. Committing it undoes
# the opacity entirely: the artifact's agg.<hex> keys become readable again and
# the reader learns which physics the policy weights. The salt is worse — it
# regenerates the whole legend from a guessed wordlist.
*term_legend*.json
*.legend.json
policy/legend*
.term_salt
*.salt
ml/runs/
